type":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Mixed umbrella (ETF and non-ETF sub-funds):** The umbrella's name does not need to include \"UCITS ETF\". Each ETF sub-fund must carry the identifier in its name and in its prospectus/supplement, KID and marketing communications. Non-ETF sub-funds must not use it, and documents should clearly separate the two.\n\n**Sub-fund with listed and unlisted classes:** The Central Bank of Ireland allows ETF status at share-class level. In that case, the identifier goes in the **name of the listed (ETF) classes**, not the sub-fund name, so unlisted classes are not described as ETFs. The supplement should make clear which classes are ETF classes and which are not, and explain any differences in dealing, such as primary-market access versus direct subscription and redemption.\n\n**Key point:** A whole-ETF sub-fund is identified at sub-fund level. A mixed sub-fund is identified at class level. Siblings that are not ETFs, whether sub-funds or classes, are never labelled \"UCITS ETF\".\n\nCheck the latest CBI UCITS Q&A for current wording.","ttft_ms":4609,"type":"result","duration_ms":7836,"uuid":"79387521-c0c1-4878-a719-0dabb928a991","ttft_stream_ms":1584,"time_to_request_ms":64,"first_content_frame_ms":1584,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
